1
00:00:12,164 --> 00:00:16,031
Today, here's a trick
that isn't particularly dangerous,

2
00:00:16,231 --> 00:00:18,345
and within reach
once you know the forward "wheel walk"

3
00:00:18,617 --> 00:00:21,538
and maybe the "one-foot idle"
with the leg extended.

4
00:00:21,858 --> 00:00:24,298
In fact, you get
exactly the same feeling

5
00:00:24,443 --> 00:00:25,444
in the "backward wheel walk".

6
00:00:25,844 --> 00:00:28,058
But instead of pushing the tire
to go forward,

7
00:00:28,244 --> 00:00:33,084
you pull it to go backward,
which works other muscles.

8
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:35,063
So the trick is still a bit different.

9
00:00:41,137 --> 00:00:44,610
The easiest way to start the trick
is from the "idle" position.

10
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,485
Because everyone knows how to "idle".

11
00:00:48,124 --> 00:00:50,130
So, the "idle", if you're with me...

12
00:00:53,634 --> 00:00:56,003
one rock forward... one rock back...

13
00:00:56,214 --> 00:00:58,452
one rock forward... one rock back...

14
00:00:59,149 --> 00:01:02,813
one rock forward...
while I lift my foot...

15
00:01:04,887 --> 00:01:09,867
one rock back...
to bring your torso back over the saddle,

16
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:12,861
perfectly upright,
find the balance point,

17
00:01:13,354 --> 00:01:16,381
and at that moment,
put your foot on the tire.

18
00:01:17,487 --> 00:01:20,734
To get back on the pedals,
do the same as when you ride forward:

19
00:01:21,587 --> 00:01:23,474
bring one foot toward the pedals.

20
00:01:24,214 --> 00:01:26,862
If your foot lands right on the pedal,

21
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:31,656
ride off, depending on your body position
and balance,

22
00:01:31,722 --> 00:01:34,293
either forward or backward,
whichever is easiest at that moment.

23
00:01:35,907 --> 00:01:38,419
But there are often situations

24
00:01:38,450 --> 00:01:40,629
where your foot lands
and doesn't find the pedal,

25
00:01:40,653 --> 00:01:41,653
or the pedal is in the wrong place,

26
00:01:41,921 --> 00:01:43,768
and then, with your foot on the tire,

27
00:01:44,047 --> 00:01:48,227
rub it a bit
to roll the wheel back a little more,

28
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:51,735
so the pedal moves
to a better spot under your foot.

29
00:01:51,801 --> 00:01:54,968
To wrap up,
here are a few things I like to do.

30
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:59,120
First, the "180 spin mount",
with the foot circling around.

31
00:02:03,377 --> 00:02:05,970
It's quite pretty,
and really satisfying to do.

32
00:02:07,244 --> 00:02:09,293
You can also go straight
into the "backward wheel walk"

33
00:02:09,317 --> 00:02:10,317
from riding backward.

34
00:02:17,034 --> 00:02:20,080
Or, while riding, do a half turn,

35
00:02:22,774 --> 00:02:26,527
and then continue
in a "backward wheel walk".

36
00:02:27,507 --> 00:02:31,212
And to finish, the transition
from the forward "wheel walk"

37
00:02:31,244 --> 00:02:32,300
to the "backward wheel walk".

38
00:02:33,074 --> 00:02:35,495
I don't do it directly.
I put one foot on the pedal.

39
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:37,967
Plus, this way, it looks
like you're stopping, but you're not.

40
00:02:40,301 --> 00:02:41,968
I'm counting on you
to work on this trick,

41
00:02:42,014 --> 00:02:48,640
and maybe make a tutorial
to help everyone improve.

42
00:02:50,441 --> 00:02:51,880
Big hugs, see you soon!

